# SpotterAI environment variables
# ---------------------------------
# Copy this file to ".env" (which is git-ignored) and paste in your own key.
#
# Get a FREE Gemini API key — no credit card required — at:
#   https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
#
# The key is read ONLY by the serverless functions and is never exposed to the
# browser.

GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# OPTIONAL — Groq is a free, separate-capacity fallback for TEXT features (plan,
# coach, food/quick-log estimates). When Gemini is rate-limited or down, requests
# fall back to Groq so the AI keeps working. Leave blank to run Gemini-only.
# Free key (no card): https://console.groq.com/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key_here
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile   # override the default model if needed
#
# Calendar export and the on-screen rest timer are fully on-device and need NO
# environment variables. The booked rest NOTIFICATION (the one that reaches a
# locked phone) is optional and needs the block below.

# OPTIONAL — booked rest-timer push. Leave ALL of these unset and the app keeps
# its page-alive alarm (sound + on-screen timer, notification while the app is
# open); nothing is half-enabled. Set the five required ones and a rest's end is booked with
# QStash at arm time, which calls /api/rest-push back at the deadline to send a
# Web Push. Free: QStash's free tier is 1,000 messages/day, no card.
#
# 1. VAPID keys (one-time):   npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
# 2. Subject: a mailto: or https: URL the push services can contact you at.
# 3. QStash: https://console.upstash.com/qstash -> the token and BOTH signing
#    keys ("current" and "next"; the next one exists so a rotation never drops
#    a rest mid-set).
# WEB_PUSH_PUBLIC_KEY=B...
# WEB_PUSH_PRIVATE_KEY=...
# WEB_PUSH_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com
# QSTASH_TOKEN=...
# QSTASH_CURRENT_SIGNING_KEY=sig_...
# QSTASH_NEXT_SIGNING_KEY=sig_...        # optional: only widens accepted signatures during a rotation
#
# OPTIONAL — the origin QStash calls back. On Vercel this is read from the
# platform's own VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL and you do not need to set it.
# Set it when self-hosting or serving from a custom domain. It is NEVER read
# from a request header: that would let a caller aim the callback anywhere.
# REST_PUSH_ORIGIN=https://your-domain.example

# OPTIONAL — Safety Lab production telemetry. A Firebase service account JSON,
# pasted as one line. Only api/audit-telemetry.js reads it, and it is never
# exposed to the browser.
#
# Leave it unset and the endpoint accepts requests and writes nothing, so local
# development and CI need no setup at all. Without it the Safety Lab simply
# omits its production block rather than showing a misleading zero.
#
# Firebase console -> Project settings -> Service accounts -> Generate new key.
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT={"type":"service_account","project_id":"..."}

# OPTIONAL — Sentry error reporting for the serverless functions.
#
# Leave it unset and lib/sentry-server.js reports nothing, so local development
# and CI need no setup. The browser half reads its DSN from the <meta
# name="sentry-dsn"> tag in index.html instead, because there is no build step
# to substitute an env var into a static page.
#
# Sentry -> Settings -> Projects -> [project] -> Client Keys (DSN).
# SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@<org>.ingest.us.sentry.io/<project-id>
